1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,166
The 15 minutes you save by skipping the spec,

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,369
become a 3-hour debug bill.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,016
Document-Driven Development fixes that before the first line of code.

4
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:22,929
First, the business core: who uses it, the real flow, the rules, the exceptions. Agreed in plain words.

5
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:29,825
Then check what already exists. Use it, adapt it, or build.

6
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:36,423
Write short documents: intent, spec, plan. Only what the code can't show.

7
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:43,900
Prove it. Every acceptance criterion becomes a check, and one command runs them all.

8
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,706
Every bug becomes a new check.

9
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:53,984
A small change is two sentences and a check run. A new product gets the full flow.

10
00:00:55,300 --> 00:01:01,627
The person knows the business. The agent knows how to build. The documents are where they meet.

11
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:06,300
Slow at the start. Fast throughout.

12
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:10,356
Works with any agent. Install it in one command.
